# Compatibility with the files and programs people already have (plan §8).
#
# WHAT THIS LIST IS FOR
# ---------------------
# 40-applications.list.chroot chooses the programs; this list makes their *content*
# work: the codecs a video needs, the sandbox plumbing an app store needs, and the
# layer that runs Windows software. Each group below explains itself.
#
# Nothing here downloads anything at build time or at boot. The Flatpak remote added by
# 0900-compat.hook.chroot is a pointer the user chooses to follow.

# --- Media codecs -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Debian's main archive carries free codecs; libavcodec-extra is the full compilation,
# including the formats Debian still redistributes. This is what makes MP4/H.265/MP3
# "just play" in parole, mpv and Firefox.
libavcodec-extra
ffmpeg
gstreamer1.0-libav
gstreamer1.0-plugins-bad
gstreamer1.0-plugins-ugly
# DVD reading and menus for mpv/parole. libdvdnav4 pulls the DVD read library at the
# soname the release actually ships; the time_t transition renamed the library package
# (t64), so naming it here would pin a name the next transition changes again.
libdvdnav4
# NOTE: CSS (commercial DVD) decryption is libdvdcss, which Debian does not carry.
# AstraOS does not ship it; a user who needs it installs it themselves, and
# docs/KNOWN_LIMITATIONS.md records the gap.

# --- Flatpak: applications outside the Debian archive ------------------------------
# Flatpak itself, plus the portal and keyring pieces a sandboxed application needs to
# show a file chooser, follow the desktop theme, and keep its secrets.
flatpak
xdg-desktop-portal
xdg-desktop-portal-gtk
gnome-keyring
libpam-gnome-keyring

# --- Windows software ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Wine runs 64-bit Windows applications out of the box. 32-bit applications need the
# i386 architecture enabled first ("dpkg --add-architecture i386" then install wine32);
# that is documented rather than preinstalled because it roughly doubles the download
# for the minority of 32-bit programs. winetricks supplies the runtime pieces many of
# them expect, on the user's explicit request.
wine
winetricks

# --- Everyday compatibility ---------------------------------------------------------
# Double-click installation of a downloaded .deb.
gdebi
# System snapshots: the undo button for everything below is a good idea.
timeshift
# The system information tool every bug report asks for.
inxi
# Text-to-speech backend for the screen reader (orca, 30-desktop) and spd-say.
speech-dispatcher
